{"id":"7d2558e2-581e-4b0d-8b69-f97074c43287","expr":"!result.contains(\"$\")","rationale":"Package names cannot contain '$', which is used for inner classes in class names.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.213982689Z"}
{"id":"35b65fe6-0d58-4054-92cf-857b03d9705f","expr":"(fqClassName.contains(\".\") || result.isEmpty())","rationale":"The method returns either the substring before the last dot or empty if no dot is present.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.224873093Z"}
{"id":"88f13d37-928e-4808-a2ae-1b09658f14d8","expr":"(!fqClassName.contains(\".\") || fqClassName.startsWith(result))","rationale":"If fqClassName contains a dot, the package name (result) is the prefix before last dot.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.224873093Z"}
{"id":"de81e663-8536-4404-b998-142981e95b13","expr":"(!result.isEmpty() || !fqClassName.contains(\".\"))","rationale":"If no dot present, result is empty string.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.224873093Z"}
{"id":"e6e13bab-38a1-4d95-bfa7-6b6295c21952","expr":"(result.length() <= fqClassName.length())","rationale":"The result is either substring of fqClassName or empty, so length cannot exceed fqClassName length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.224873093Z"}
{"id":"786c1085-7b59-4390-9469-0116f553b197","expr":"(fqClassName.length() == 0  || (result + fqClassName.substring(result.length() + 1)).equals(fqClassName))","rationale":"Given fqClassName like 'package.name.Class', result returns the package name part before last dot.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.224873093Z"}
{"id":"70d7fe8a-4cb7-4afc-af53-d51595185ce8","expr":"fqClassName != null","rationale":"This is required by the Assert.notNull call at the beginning of the method.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.230006709Z"}
{"id":"26a0e43f-618a-4547-acd8-7ce65e05d908","expr":"fqClassName.length() >= 0","rationale":"By definition, the length of a string is non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.230006709Z"}
{"id":"2bc77fdf-0f0f-4fce-9b9d-6b1acfa8b365","expr":"fqClassName.contains(\".\") || fqClassName.indexOf('.') == -1","rationale":"This reflects the possibility that the fully qualified class name either has or does not have the package separator.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.230006709Z"}
{"id":"a72dde3b-5b08-47c7-b797-c05f5d56ee21","expr":"fqClassName.indexOf('.') >= -1","rationale":"The indexOf method returns -1 if not found or a valid index >= 0.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.230006709Z"}
{"id":"ca7f404d-1d18-469a-a38e-c53b2c3f91c4","expr":"fqClassName.length() > 0","rationale":"While not explicitly stated, it is reasonable to expect fqClassName is not empty.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getPackageName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.230006709Z"}
{"id":"050fddc9-511c-4af9-9e34-c2f3ea1c9046","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"The method asserts that clazz is not null at entry.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.233132554Z"}
{"id":"ad779732-9af0-4731-a6b1-45d31d3fdc93","expr":"clazz.getCanonicalName() == null || clazz.getCanonicalName().equals(clazz.getName()) == false","rationale":"The canonical name may be null only for local or anonymous classes, otherwise it's a valid string different from simple name.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.233132554Z"}
{"id":"cd267260-729b-466d-927f-4feaafae77f9","expr":"clazz.getCanonicalName() == null || clazz.getCanonicalName().contains(\".\")","rationale":"Canonical class names typically include package names separated by dots.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.233132554Z"}
{"id":"ffccb9a8-8189-4f01-b7d9-e0579c47ebe3","expr":"clazz.getCanonicalName() == null || clazz.isMemberClass() || clazz.getCanonicalName().equals(clazz.getSimpleName()) == false","rationale":"If the canonical name is non-null and the class is a member class, the canonical name differs from the simple name.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.233132554Z"}
{"id":"0085a72b-7033-4b98-8e41-d248cad93473","expr":"clazz.getCanonicalName() == null || clazz.getCanonicalName().equals(clazz.getTypeName()) == false","rationale":"The method returns canonicalName if non-null, else typeName, showing these two differ in such cases.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.233132554Z"}
{"id":"ddeda04c-e65a-4502-9ac4-834589772aa0","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"The parameter clazz must not be null as asserted in the method.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getClassFileName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.234001871Z"}
{"id":"021e9c08-6868-4e99-9c00-bdf5aebacc37","expr":"clazz.getName() != null","rationale":"The class name returned by getName() is always non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getClassFileName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.234001871Z"}
{"id":"ef54ea9b-dfb7-4442-bff9-e5c3f131a75c","expr":"clazz.getName().contains(\".\") == (clazz.getName().lastIndexOf('.') >= 0)","rationale":"If the class name contains a dot, the lastIndexOf the dot is non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getClassFileName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.234001871Z"}
{"id":"e6ae5c86-120b-43ae-8f64-d92fdb930f71","expr":"clazz.getName().substring(clazz.getName().lastIndexOf('.') + 1).length() > 0","rationale":"The simple class name part (after last dot) is non-empty string.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getClassFileName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.234001871Z"}
{"id":"be805837-f247-4c59-97cb-5a2957dd6d47","expr":"clazz.getName().endsWith(clazz.getSimpleName())","rationale":"Fully qualified class name ends with its simple class name.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getClassFileName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.234001871Z"}
{"id":"c218121c-d94d-4180-b298-d769ee5a84a3","expr":"result != null","rationale":"Since the method returns canonicalName if non-null, otherwise clazz.getTypeName(), both of which are non-null strings, result cannot be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.244289890Z"}
{"id":"673eb8ed-1daf-4f24-9755-d7dc7ebd9790","expr":"result.equals(clazz.getCanonicalName()) || result.equals(clazz.getTypeName())","rationale":"The method returns canonicalName if not null else clazz.getTypeName(), so result matches one of them.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.244289890Z"}
{"id":"ff06d4ef-93cf-4679-8d36-6af0cd6c5100","expr":"clazz.getCanonicalName() == null || result.equals(clazz.getCanonicalName())","rationale":"The ternary expression (canonicalName!=null ? canonicalName : typeName) enforces this invariant.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.244289890Z"}
{"id":"d8ad28ab-05b4-4a0d-b91f-bc6f81fa3a13","expr":"result.length() > 0","rationale":"Both canonicalName and typeName are non-empty string representations of class name, so result must have positive length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getCanonicalName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.244289890Z"}
{"id":"c446b300-be8a-473c-adc4-c39337a41fca","expr":"clazz != null","rationale":"Method contract asserts clazz must not be null before execution.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.245359163Z"}
{"id":"34702b57-98e9-4f0b-ba24-794b626648da","expr":"clazz.getSimpleName() != null","rationale":"Since clazz is non-null, getSimpleName() returns non-null string.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.245359163Z"}
{"id":"fdbc4809-34e9-4e01-82b5-1dcfd2e0a81a","expr":"clazz.getName() != null","rationale":"getName() returns a non-null fully qualified name for the class object.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.245359163Z"}
{"id":"73736773-816a-4325-8a59-77b7c701797c","expr":"clazz.getTypeName() != null","rationale":"getTypeName() returns the qualified name string, which is non-null when clazz is non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.245359163Z"}
{"id":"59f2efd6-e919-4af9-b377-5de531b72aea","expr":"clazz.getModifiers() >= 0","rationale":"The modifiers bit mask is always a non-negative integer.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.245359163Z"}
{"id":"b9283531-8833-4036-a93a-bf418bbc412a","expr":"className != null && className.length() > 0","rationale":"The method asserts the className is not empty, so it must be non-null and have length > 0.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getShortName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.233610253Z"}
{"id":"78f16d65-7317-4b36-a272-6dc76aa5e573","expr":"className.indexOf('.') >= -1","rationale":"The indexOf call checks for PACKAGE_SEPARATOR in className, which may or may not be present.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getShortName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.233610253Z"}
{"id":"f82612d3-6201-4b79-8098-388c5ce62987","expr":"className.indexOf('$') >= -1","rationale":"The className may or may not contain CGLIB_CLASS_SEPARATOR which is used to determine name end.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getShortName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.233610253Z"}
{"id":"757b8c15-dcce-4e47-a1e8-c30d80ecd4c4","expr":"className.lastIndexOf('.') >= -1","rationale":"The method uses lastIndexOf PACKAGE_SEPARATOR which can be -1 if no dot is present.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getShortName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.233610253Z"}
{"id":"3beb6d04-8591-418a-8df3-52f5af678b3b","expr":"className.contains(\"$\") || !className.contains(\"$\")","rationale":"This indicates if CGLIB_CLASS_SEPARATOR is present or not; it is either true or false.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getShortName(String):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.233610253Z"}
{"id":"0596c9ba-5efb-4682-9e6b-ec0379175534","expr":"result.equals(clazz.getTypeName())","rationale":"The method returns clazz.getTypeName(), so result must equal clazz.getTypeName().","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.256569239Z"}
{"id":"88ee71ec-7c2b-47bc-9612-b6d2443d156a","expr":"result.endsWith(\".class\")","rationale":"The method appends CLASS_FILE_SUFFIX which equals \".class\" to the class simple name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getClassFileName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.259566773Z"}
{"id":"fb1d8259-4be9-450b-98bc-536cb56e8c04","expr":"clazz.getName().endsWith(result.substring(0, result.length() - \".class\".length()))","rationale":"Since result is the class simple name plus \".class\", the class full name ends with that simple name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getClassFileName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.259566773Z"}
{"id":"aac1cabb-4e2b-4a93-a49c-897e4b1fc2c8","expr":"clazz.getName().indexOf('.') < 0 || result.startsWith(clazz.getName().substring(clazz.getName().lastIndexOf('.') + 1))","rationale":"result is the simple name + \".class\", so result starts with the simple class name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getClassFileName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.259566773Z"}
{"id":"dd8977ab-2c50-4ac5-997a-2c943a95401d","expr":"result.length() == clazz.getSimpleName().length() + \".class\".length()","rationale":"The result is the simple name plus \".class\", so lengths match.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getClassFileName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.259566773Z"}
{"id":"9e807193-e679-493e-a666-823ae9e81fb3","expr":"clazz != null && result != null","rationale":"clazz is not null due to assert, and result is non-null as a substring concatenation.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getClassFileName(Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.259566773Z"}
{"id":"33b1c6e6-c757-41fe-b540-47274953c7fc","expr":"method != null && method.getName() != null && !method.getName().isEmpty()","rationale":"The method must be non-null and have a non-empty name, as the qualified method name depends on its name.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.260871019Z"}
{"id":"e05e7c8c-9b3f-4b7f-aebf-cd87c06283d2","expr":"method.getDeclaringClass() != null","rationale":"The Method must have a non-null declaring class, which is essential for forming the qualified method name.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.260871019Z"}
{"id":"4d269541-f355-4425-8711-c12add878cbf","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The method likely returns a non-null qualified method name string.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.263233286Z"}
{"id":"7c22dcbc-73bf-4838-8eec-8b7d93d6ef83","expr":"result.contains(\".\")","rationale":"Qualified method name includes class name and method name, separated by a dot.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.263233286Z"}
{"id":"9d72d5b7-1efd-469c-986d-803e7451ec94","expr":"result.endsWith(method.getName())","rationale":"Qualified method name string ends with the method's actual name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.263233286Z"}
{"id":"5e667081-d440-4791-880f-135b498e22bc","expr":"result.startsWith(method.getDeclaringClass().getName())","rationale":"Qualified method name begins with the fully-qualified name of the declaring class.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.263233286Z"}
{"id":"17ca628a-cdf0-4a28-b8a0-0a792c7b4285","expr":"result.startsWith(clazz != null ? clazz.getName() : method.getDeclaringClass().getName())","rationale":"The returned string is composed of the class name, a dot, and the method name, so it should start with the class name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.275057057Z"}
{"id":"cbb84083-8ff2-4b89-93ad-2ad304749b4e","expr":"result.endsWith(method.getName())","rationale":"The returned qualified method name ends with the method's name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.275057057Z"}
{"id":"f6a5b134-40af-4b0a-9c1e-2157a880f9e3","expr":"result.contains(\".\")","rationale":"Since the return value concatenates class name and method name with a dot, it must contain a dot.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.275057057Z"}
{"id":"0a039a32-99f9-4328-96c0-e0915e1e9944","expr":"(clazz == null || clazz == method.getDeclaringClass() || result.startsWith(clazz.getName()))","rationale":"If clazz is not null and different from method's declaring class, the result starts with clazz's name.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.275057057Z"}
{"id":"e55499e0-934e-4a0b-984c-5be5e26bc97a","expr":"result.equals((clazz != null ? clazz : method.getDeclaringClass()).getName() + '.' + method.getName())","rationale":"The result equals the class name (clazz or method's declaring class) plus a dot plus method name, exactly.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getQualifiedMethodName(Method,Class<?>):String","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.275057057Z"}
{"id":"5f40cc99-dfef-48d9-a263-13c12c9037be","expr":"clazz != null && paramTypes != null && clazz.getDeclaredConstructors() != null","rationale":"At method entry, clazz must be non-null to search for constructors, and paramTypes represents the constructor parameter types.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasConstructor(Class<?>,Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.276161497Z"}
{"id":"b7619e04-e98b-4805-b796-93077ba997b3","expr":"paramTypes.getClass().isArray()","rationale":"paramTypes is an array of Class objects representing constructor parameter types.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasConstructor(Class<?>,Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.276161497Z"}
{"id":"c6380d05-1761-4d9d-8db5-c82d927aedca","expr":"clazz.isAssignableFrom(clazz)","rationale":"Any class is assignable from itself; this is a meaningful basic property of clazz.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasConstructor(Class<?>,Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.276161497Z"}
{"id":"f9faa061-87a6-4753-9729-f5a01edaa2a6","expr":"clazz.isInterface() == false","rationale":"While not always guaranteed, generally constructors are found in concrete classes, so clazz.isInterface() being false is expected.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#hasConstructor(Class<?>,Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:08.276161497Z"}
