{"id":"b6414f1b-645f-4f69-a95b-f8198679877e","expr":"type != null","rationale":"The method of expects a Class parameter named type; it is typical that this parameter should not be null to create a valid TypeReference.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.TypeReference#of(Class<?>):TypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/TypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:14.440244046Z"}
{"id":"83873b6e-f5d2-4bce-b39b-1360809f9ace","expr":"type.isPrimitive() || !type.isPrimitive()","rationale":"The parameter type is a Class object; it can represent either a primitive type or a reference type, so it is always true and not a useful invariant, so excluded.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.TypeReference#of(Class<?>):TypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/TypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:14.440244046Z"}
{"id":"4a7d0ea7-dbb1-42ae-8f19-73cc2cc5f8db","expr":"type.isArray() == (type.getComponentType() != null)","rationale":"In Java, if a class is an array type, getComponentType() returns the component Class; otherwise it returns null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.TypeReference#of(Class<?>):TypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/TypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:14.440244046Z"}
{"id":"0a1a016d-f9ce-4d87-b940-a3e0fa73cabe","expr":"!type.isPrimitive() || !type.isArray()","rationale":"A Class object cannot represent both a primitive type and an array type simultaneously.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.aot.hint.TypeReference#of(Class<?>):TypeReference","file":"org/springframework/aot/hint/TypeReference.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:14.440244046Z"}
