{"id":"3ae8723a-40bc-413f-8fad-da22a15a99b5","expr":"result.getSort() != -1","rationale":"ASM Type sort values are non-negative integers representing the kind of type.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Method):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:17.629689050Z"}
{"id":"f08b3368-9518-416f-8013-60c6a9e451e9","expr":"typeDescriptor != null && typeDescriptor.length() > 0","rationale":"The method uses typeDescriptor.length(), so typeDescriptor must be non-null. Also, it makes sense that typeDescriptor has positive length to represent a type descriptor.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(String):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:17.626808226Z"}
{"id":"2c532498-7ca5-453c-b38c-34063f7b7a87","expr":"typeDescriptor.length() >= 1","rationale":"Type descriptor length must be at least 1 to avoid errors.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(String):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:17.626808226Z"}
{"id":"bf2edb3e-eb1f-491e-af29-f6466cd7a5fe","expr":"method != null && method.getName() != null && method.getReturnType() != null && method.getParameterTypes() != null","rationale":"The method parameter is passed to getMethodDescriptor, which requires a valid method with non-null parts.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.Type#getType(Method):Type","file":"org/springframework/asm/Type.java","createdAt":"2026-09-08T06:23:17.629880932Z"}
